MailPostA's own code is the scripts, configuration templates, container
setup and documentation in this repository. It is not a fork: it builds a
container image around the following projects, which are downloaded at build
time and used unmodified. Each keeps its own license.

  himalaya (email CLI, Rust)
    https://github.com/pimalaya/himalaya
    Copyright (c) the Pimalaya project and himalaya contributors
    Licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License 2.0, at your option.
    The official release binary is bundled in the image; its license files
    are in /usr/share/doc/himalaya/ inside the image.

  isync / mbsync (IMAP sync)
    https://isync.sourceforge.io/
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v2 or later.
    Installed from Debian; license in /usr/share/doc/isync/copyright.

  notmuch (mail index and tags)
    https://notmuchmail.org/
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3 or later.
    Installed from Debian; license in /usr/share/doc/notmuch/copyright.

  Caddy (web server, used for the web UI login)
    https://caddyserver.com/
    Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
    Used as the official docker.io/library/caddy image.

  Debian, Python, PyYAML and the other Debian packages in the image keep
  their own licenses (see /usr/share/doc/*/copyright inside the image).

